{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385461-what-should-the-role-of-thin-bloods-be","id":1385461,"title":"What should the role of Thin Bloods be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-03T14:41:23-07:00","id":1385461,"title":"What should the role of Thin Bloods be?","content":"Just curious how you handle them in your game and how important they should be, setting-wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T14:52:23-07:00","id":1385463,"title":"","content":"Possible Roles:<br /> A sign of change.<br /> A sign of The End.<br /> The disenfranchised group that other oppressed groups look at and think, &quot;At least I am not them.&quot;<br /> A test of how devoted the thick blooded Anarachs are to their ideals.<br /> Free agents.<br /> A vulnerability to Kindred society as a whole.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T16:25:35-07:00","id":1385476,"title":"","content":"in the Cam, they're a source of employment for the scourges, and a way to justify the fascist policies of the sect<br /> <br /> in the Sabbat, they're a reminder of cainite inequality in the blood, and a good incentive for spreading diablerie culture (you are encouraged to diablerize before embracing anyone, less you risk siring weak bloods, which is kinda social suicide in the sect)<br /> <br /> they're also good material for vicissitude/thaumaturgical experimentation,<br /> and food for mythology and all kinds of wild religious speculation (some zealots will want to capture them for what they might represent)<br /> <br /> the seers are an interesting plot device for ambitious vampires (elder or otherwise)<br /> <br /> and...well most of this is in the books and I can't think of original uses.<br /> I guess I lack creativity<br /> damn you thin bloods for reminding me how much I suck","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T17:30:58-07:00","id":1385486,"title":"","content":"The primary place where thin-blooded come up in my game is as a deceased parent since one of the PCs is a dhampir (who, thanks to the pale aura merit, is passing themselves off as a 13th Gen Brujah fledging surprisingly well, for now) who, after learning their vampire father was killed by the Scourge, is trying to get close to enact revenge.<br /> <br /> Since I\u2019m pretty much, \u201cGehenna\u2019s not all that immanent,\u201d the main way they\u2019re coming up is in relation to how the Anarchs\u2019 casual embracing is straining the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also a secret agenda that the Scourge\u2019s motives are that they sired a Caitiff (despite the Scourge being 9th Generation) that they abandoned in shame and that Caitiff went on to sire a bunch more down into the thin-blooded generations that are causing the Prince problems with the Masquerade. The Scourge is determined to \u201cclean up her mess\u201d before anyone can figure out which vampire is responsible for the \u201cCaitiff infestation.\u201d<br /> <br /> So mostly I\u2019m using the Thin-Blooded as just the latest affront to the Prince\u2019s right to control the creation of progeny because the Caitiff now outnumber the Clans in the city now largely because of those thin-bloods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T19:09:38-07:00","id":1385507,"title":"","content":"For me personally, I use them in a number of ways, with the main spectrums being focused on politics, society, and mysticism.<br /> <br /> \u2022Mystical<br /> Mysticism is the easiest to dig into as elders and Noddists consider the thin-blooded to be harbingers of Gehenna. The fact that the curse seems to be growing thin represents an approaching event horizon, that the center cannot hold. So they try to fight back by desperately warding off this Time of Judgment by destroying the thin-blooded, unknowingly drawing the cataclysm closer as the destruction of the blood causes the sleeping elders to stir in torpor.<br /> <br /> With other mystical traditions aside from Noddism, I can see really three roads of consideration. Either ignoring thin-bloods (not hard given the position of certain sects), considering them an ill omen if your creed treats the vampiric tradition with reverence-as such an obviously weak and malformed example of the curse must reflect some spiritual failing, or alternatively those seeking a path towards redemption or some other higher ideal might see high gen and thin-bloods as an avenue of their pursuit, perhaps even a sign of a coming liberation from the eternal night.<br /> <br /> \u2022Political <br /> The thin-blooded are often young, high generation, and a not insignificant percentage are illegally embraced. Each sect is going to treat this vampiric population differently and the thin-blooded can be used as a strong allegory for the disadvantaged.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is theoretically built upon total inclusion yet the existence of the scourge belies that and reveals the truth. The elders and the Inner Circle fear the thin-bloods. They may justify the scourge's practices by saying that thin-bloods are illegally embraced or that they represent potential breaches of the masquerade or that they must be eliminated to ensure the health of the vampiric community (some older kindred have a hard time letting go of eugenics). Yet these are all justifications for the reality that thin-bloods are outcasts and viciously hunted down out of both mysticism and from those pragmatic enough to eliminate competition that no one will bother them for destroying.<br /> <br /> I forget how sources describe the Sabbat'a opinion of the thin-bloods but I must imagine that it can't be that good. However, the Sabbat does offer one alternative route to the thin-blooded aside from destruction: devour your enemies and become potent. Those who can be brought about to this way of thinking are likely to become True Sabbat, those who refuse are likely to become fodder for feeding and training the Sword of Caine.<br /> <br /> The Anarch Movement almost certainly has a broad spectrum of opinions, but they're probably a thin-bloods best shot. They are less likely to harbor the noddist prejudices of the elders or to be as frenzied as the Sabbat. Even then, I imagine many would struggle to gain a position of strength given the predatory nature of some vampires, even as I'm sure that some Anarchs would go out of their way to welcome Caitiff and Thin-Bloods alike into their ranks.<br /> <br /> \u2022Socially<br /> I tend to treat Thin-Bloods and Caitiff, particularly given their co-morbidity, to be in similar camps. They survive as autarkis by claiming domains nobody else wants and either flying under the radar or grouping together for strength. Some roam or hide alone, likely largely ignorant of kindred society. Others might band together in barrens or suburbs in what I usually call 'Colonies'. One thin-blood is easy pickings. A dozen banded together in an abandoned factory are harder to smoke out.<br /> <br /> I ultimately treat thin-bloods as another spectrum of vampiric society. The unlucky and the outcasts. The desperate pariahs who have to fight to even survive. Their very existence underlines the villainy of the other sects and the complicit villainy of any kindred who participates in them. Perhaps that Toreador is perfectly nice, but by participating within Camarilla society, they tacitly accept the sect's rite to hunt down and destroy thin-bloods and Caitiff for the crime of existing.<br /> <br /> That is the condition of the thin-bloods and to me they represent one of the purest representations of what Vampire being a Gothic-Punk setting really means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T22:23:40-07:00","id":1386260,"title":"","content":"Something for the Anarchs and the Cammies to fight over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T07:51:39-07:00","id":1386399,"title":"","content":"Bloodbags for hungry Methuselah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T07:57:10-07:00","id":1386402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385461-what-should-the-role-of-thin-bloods-be#post1385461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious how you handle them in your game and how important they should be, setting-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>An &quot;x factor,&quot; in that they defy vampire understanding of themselves, their biology, and how the world works. Something to remind everyone that, as the Yankovic song goes, &quot;everything you know is wrong.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T08:27:12-07:00","id":1387730,"title":"","content":"Usually, they're a threat, because the Camarilla doesn't want to bring them into the fold as true vampires; they're more like masterless ghouls. They both know too much to and too little. Camarilla princes like giving violent fledglings/neonates the opertunity to evict thinbloods in order to foster a sense of beloning; This act says &quot;You neonates are better than them&quot; and also &quot;you neonates are just as bad as we are/this is the natural order of things&quot; and in return the prince will give them a pat on the back and maybe a minor parcel of land/the right to make a ghoul or something like that.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of thinbloods is a casual matter of course, a mercy even. The liability outweighs the benefit of keeping them alive, and they weren't going to have a happy unlife anyway. The real concern is finding who sired them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-12-2020, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T09:47:28-07:00","id":1387747,"title":"","content":"&quot;Thin-bloods are like any other vampire. They're either a benefit or a hazard. If they're a benefit, it's not my problem.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T14:42:17-07:00","id":1387811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385461-what-should-the-role-of-thin-bloods-be#post1385461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious how you handle them in your game and how important they should be, setting-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The downtrodden masses of vampiredom, those who even the weakest of vampires feel they are beneath them, also those who have broken the curse of Caine and are potentially free from the jyhad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T21:44:33-07:00","id":1387899,"title":"","content":"I had a joke answer earlier in the thread, but on further reflection I can see Thin-Bloods serving as characters whose tragedy is that they were embraced too late, long after (what they imagine as) the best years of the vampire have been squandered. They can be the equivalent of a mortal Lost Generation, a sign of decline and diminishing opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T02:59:40-07:00","id":1387969,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>LEANDROS VAMPIRE SOCIETY OVERHAUL</b></span></span><br /> I use Thin Bloods as part of the bulk of the vampire doom , yes they make the bulk of vampire society despite being the underdogs.But why well let\u00b4s talk about the power of age and how the embrace works...<ul><li>Generation no longer exist blood potency is measured by age (this makes gehena a myth and source of expeculation)</li> <li>Embrace cost XP depending of how much Starting Blood Potency you want ranging from Thin Blood to 5BP</li> <li>Thin Bloods cannot embrace and you cannot never embrace someone of equal blood potency.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Thin Blood Capabilies</b><ul><li>They can sunwalk as long as they mantain their humanity high enought</li> <li>They cannot use discipline unless they got certain merit and never above 3 (Blood Magic being the exception due to being some kind of science/edge magic)</li> <li>They can be reembraced and this is used as a bait to ensure their loyalty as it is cheaper to reembrace than embrace</li> <li>They can also become true vampires if they comit diablerie and can go back to human if they</li> <li>They can spend blood for the purpouse of healing as if they were a blood potency 1 vampire.</li> <li>They don\u00b4t halve damage/considerate bullets lethals , piercing objets agravated.</li> <li>They can become human again if his sire dies within the first month of the transformation</li> </ul><br /> <b>How this affect them</b><br /> They are still pariah due they being the weakest vampires , on the other hand due the harship of vampire society killing a lot of his members , the need of replacement and the rise of younger low potency vampires means that in the XXI century Thin Bloods are the most numerous kind of vampire and must be taken into account for fear of them becoming anarchs so some of them are integrated into the vampire society as if they where self-sustaining ghouls.<br /> <br /> The fact that they can be reembraced makes them wonderful pawns so it is not rare that some elder steals the failed progeny of his rival to get an asset.However a lot of them are executed for masquerade breaches or pused by hunter before they can join the vampire society not to menti\u00f3n their sire wanting to kill them for shame or to avoid the prince reprisal.So in certain way a thin blood can find some way in the camarilla , the anarch or the sabbath making them more player friendly but they need a patron behind their backs.<br /> <br /> This change in design makes a coterie of thin bloods a great game option that can operate in various kind of games (Anarch/Camarilla/sabbat).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T07:17:49-07:00","id":1388039,"title":"","content":"Another thing about thinbloods. <br /> <br /> Vampires don't want vampires around that haven't gone through a sire's tutalage. They're a risk to the masquerade and can start causing unfortunate questions to be asked. The overwhelming majority of 14th/15th gens are mistakes that sires realise and abandon; No prince is giving a 13th gen permision to embrace, many princes in europe consider 12th gen the limit and 13th thin blooded, whilst some ancients are shocked at double digits as a whole. <br /> <br /> But adopting some thin blood you found dumped in your yard is kinda like being cucked; worse, it's risky. What if that thin blood's a trap? There you are thinking you've got a new retainer, but What if some vampire left in in your yard, set up a blood bond or some dominate, and your new thin blood retainer murders you in your sleep? What if they want to become a &quot;real&quot; vampire? What if some authority figure thinks <i>you</i> sired or aranged for the thin blood and you're trying to get around the law? There's only 1/2 or 1/4 of a chance to survive a thinblood embrace; maybe killing one is just doing what nature intended. It's not a real vampire; you don't need rights of destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T13:31:49-07:00","id":1389440,"title":"","content":"I see them as an unpredictable synthesis of the vampiric curse and humanity's supernatural side. And that 'fusion' can manifest in alot of unpredictable ways because we've seen quite a few variations on the curses weakening or flaws.<br /> <br /> On one end of the spectrum you have Caitiff and something like the 14th generation - something that is in essence 'mostly' vampire (may lack some of their flaws or powers or like Caitiff may not have an origin.) This reflects more of a 'make your own vampire' approach (which is what Caitiff were meant to be.) On this end the Curse may have weakened but still dominates.<br /> <br /> On the opposite end you have the TotB Dhampirs. Basically an alternative to ghouls and revenants and something that is more 'true' to the original dhampir myths I've been able to delve into (someone who is born of a vampire and a human and may have some odd qualities or magic powers but is still basically human, rather than what fiction has turned the concept into.) The vampire heritage may awaken their supernatural nature in different ways but they're still mostly human. If I was stealing the Dhampir ideas from KtR (which I have) this is where they would fit.<br /> <br /> Then you have that broad 'middle ground' which is what 14-16th generation in ToTB and 5th edition seem to portray. This is where the vampire/human fusion will mix to varying degrees but also has the most unpredictable results (again as depicted in 5th and ToTB) and I feel is the ground where you might recreate certain 'non-traditional' views of vampires (Blade or Underworld Vampires, perhaps, or the Vampire Hunter D/Castlevania style vampire or dhampir.) KtR Revenants would fit into this category IMHO (leaning more towards the vampire side) whereas KotE Dhampyr might go here (leaning more towards the human side.) This is ultimately the realm of the filthy hybrid that WoD didn't always like but can still have a role despite that.<br /> <br /> One other difference I hold to is that the 'Thin Blood' concept isn't necessarily tied to the higher generations. Its more LIKELY to happen in higher generations, but it could happen in lower ones as well. Such as Count Dunlop from the Giovanni Chronicles who was a 6th Generation Gangrel who was a vampire who lacked the 'stasis' immortality - his body still aged and he would have been dead in around a millenia without help. Some Thin Bloods in ToTB could age at a rate of 1 year for every 20, and the earlier depictions of Revenants and Dhampyr suggested a 1 in 10 rate of aging, so it fits in with that neatly.<br /> <br /> Conversely I always felt that if Thin Bloods require twice as many BP to use certain abilities (healing, enhancing physical attributes) they should also gain nourishment more easily from humans (animals may or may not be the same bringing to mind 'Vampire Dad' from ToTB) Generally (1.5-2x more points compared to a 'normal' vampire. The opposite of older vampires or Methuselah who need vampire blood to survive.) <br /> <br /> I'll note if we're talking V5 I feel thin-blood alchemy is a bit lacking under this guise. Not bad per se, but it needs development to reflect something borrowing from human supernatural powers (like hedge magic or other numina) and vampiric power (Whether its acutal blood magic or not.) I usually tend to allow a bit of Hedge magic and Blood magic to bleed into TBA in a fashion not unlike combination disciplines. Oh and throw in some CoD Malisons or twists from 'Half Damned' because I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 05-17-2020, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T21:20:54-07:00","id":1389559,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, they\u2019re someone even further downhill for the shit to roll towards. On the other hand, they\u2019re a wild card that scares the elders. On the third hand, they can move among mortals to a degree other vampires can\u2019t, and there\u2019s a niche for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T13:30:03-07:00","id":1389740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385461-what-should-the-role-of-thin-bloods-be#post1385461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious how you handle them in your game and how important they should be, setting-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Food.<br /> <br /> No, seriously. The blood of kindred just tastes indescribably better than that of the kine, but the fact that consuming this blood creates a blood bond made it a poisoned chalice.<br /> <br /> Then the thinblooded come along and the poison goes disappears. Every vampire of note just goes out and embraces down to a thinblood (i.e. embrace, have their childe embrace, repeat, kill the vamps in between) or five, gives them a three stage bloodbond, and then uses them as blood filters.<br /> <br /> Feed the thinblood some mortal blood (crappy blood is just fine) and then feast from the thinblood. Every Elder should have a few thinbloods buried away in torpor, ready to be awakened if their filter needs to be replaced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25361-sagacious-gamer","name":"Sagacious Gamer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T13:37:56-07:00","id":1389742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagacious Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385461-what-should-the-role-of-thin-bloods-be?p=1389740#post1389740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Food.<br /> <br /> No, seriously. The blood of kindred just tastes indescribably better than that of the kine, but the fact that consuming this blood creates a blood bond made it a poisoned chalice.<br /> <br /> Then the thinblooded come along and the poison goes disappears. Every vampire of note just goes out and embraces down to a thinblood (i.e. embrace, have their childe embrace, repeat, kill the vamps in between) or five, gives them a three stage bloodbond, and then uses them as blood filters.<br /> <br /> Feed the thinblood some mortal blood (crappy blood is just fine) and then feast from the thinblood. Every Elder should have a few thinbloods buried away in torpor, ready to be awakened if their filter needs to be replaced.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've thought of a similar niche for Thin-Bloods aswell. Their basically a nothing burgher part of VTM. People even wrongly typecast them the same as Caitiff- but Caitiff are only ever Vampires with a sire that has abandoned them- if they orient themselves well, they can figure out their Clan themselves by stringing along the grapevine of Kindred society and matching what disciplines they have. Thin-Bloods though are just too flat by every imagination. Their mostly to just be used as enhanced bloodbags. Maybe thats the reason why the time of Thin-Blood is an ill omen for the VTM line, because thats when all the Meths and even Antes begin to awake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T14:02:49-07:00","id":1389746,"title":"","content":"I love the Ashefinders from Cults of the Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T10:56:52-07:00","id":1390328,"title":"","content":"Thin bloods might be better than mortals as far as taste (and better than 'servants' like Revenants or Ghouls) but they're blood is still inferior to lower generation vampires. Some might be able to feed from lower generation as a way to avoid the Blood Bond, but eventually in the traditional system stuff like Methuselah's thirst will kick in seriously and you're going to need lower generations (Heck, ToTB implied Antes were WAY past Methuselah's Thirst stage.)<br /> <br /> Also if the Withering is considered to still be a thing Thin Bloods probably wouldn't be potent enough to stave off the effects via Diablerie. <br /> <br /> Although if you assume 'Thin Blood Syndrome' can extend to lower generations like I believe it can the idea of 'Thin Blooded vitae filters' is more sustainable. There will still be diminishing returns. But they are likely beyond the scope of most player experiences and NPC interactions (the really ancient and powerful vampires.. really old 4th generation and above that are usually going to be rarer encounters.) <br /> <br /> Mind you there's the cultural issues as well pertaining diablerie and the perception of Thin Bloods in general within vampire society. In the Camarilla I could see this being an 'open secret' but still one that doesn't really lead to much acceptance of thin bloods (except perhaps in more of a V5 oriented scenario.) Sabbat might be more of a mixed bag depending on which branch of the Sabbat you talk about and beliefs (Some might be less tolerant like Camarilla vampires and possibly for the same reason. Other Sabbat may take a more egalitarian look. Or perhaps welcome the Thin Bloods because it means that the Antediluvians are about to rise up and things are going to get interesting.) I think Thin Bloods would probably most benefit from this transactional relationship amongst Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}